{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdyCbaU1wHS6udwyLNd3D","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Fix Plan\n\n1. **Root cause**: Newton iteration in `src/engine/irr.ts` accumulates floating-point error differently across Node 20 vs 22 due to optimizer differences. Deltas (1e-14 to 2e-13) are well below the 1e-9 tolerance but raw float serialization exposes them.\n\n2. **Change location**: `golden/mapper.ts`\n   - **What**: Round `irr` to 9 decimal places (matching the 1e-9 behavioral tolerance) before serialization.\n   - **Concrete change**: \n     ```typescript\n     irr: Math.round(rawIrr * 1e9) / 1e9\n     ```\n\n3. **Regenerate baseline**:\n   - Run on Node 20: `npm run golden:update`\n   - Commit the updated `golden/projections.json`\n\n4. **Verify the gate**:\n   - Run CI (both Node 20 and 22): `npm test -- --golden`\n   - Both jobs should pass; `git diff golden/projections.json` should be empty on second run.\n\n**Rationale**: The tolerance is already defined in your spec. Enforcement belongs at serialization, not in the solver. This makes the gate truly portable."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":342,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":302,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}}
